{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The voice of the lad.</b> Rashi explained: from here that the prayer of the sick is heard before the prayers of others. And as for what we say in Berakhot, 'a prisoner does not release himself from prison' — one may answer, the reason is that an ordinary sick person cannot concentrate his intention, but this one, who did concentrate — his prayer was heard before HaShem." "<b>Where he is.</b> Rashi explained: according to his deeds now. But we say that a stubborn and rebellious son is executed on account of his end. Rather, one may answer: a stubborn and rebellious son — from the outset he is wicked because of what he will become at his end; but here, from the outset Ishmael was righteous regarding that matter of bowing down to drink water, for thirst — this is what Rashi explained, according to his deeds now. <b>Where he is</b> — because she moved away from him about a bowshot's distance and did not see him, it was necessary to say 'where he is.' Another interpretation: <b>where he is</b> — even in a desert that has no water."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:10.994523537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}